Tell us more: I’d consider myself a superfan of Australian comedians because Aussie comedy is exactly my kind of humour: sharp, dry, self-aware, and slightly unhinged in the best way. I love comedians who can turn a completely normal situation into absolute chaos without trying too hard. Nobody makes a minor inconvenience sound like a national emergency quite like an Aussie comedian. I’ve been into Australian comedy since my uni days and still have a Will Anderson poster from around 2012 from the Uni Bar drinking era, plus some old Chaser merch I’ve held onto for years. I’m the kind of person who constantly sends podcast clips, quotes comedy bits in normal conversations, and ends up down random YouTube rabbit holes watching stand-up and interviews at stupid hours of the night. I’d make a fun podium superfan because I’m naturally expressive, genuinely excited by this stuff, and fully commit to the moment. Also, my partner has absolutely no idea I’m trying to come see Odeo, so being able to surprise them with this would honestly be unreal.

